WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.091
Begin with one runtime that makes the first useful workload easy.

00:00:05.091 --> 00:00:13.033
LM Studio provides a desktop interface for discovering compatible models, adjusting settings, chatting, and exposing a local API.

00:00:13.033 --> 00:00:18.531
Ollama emphasizes a simple command-line and service workflow with packaged model definitions.

00:00:18.531 --> 00:00:27.288
Both can reduce setup friction and help confirm that the hardware and driver stack work before additional components are introduced.

00:00:27.288 --> 00:00:28.306
Llama.

00:00:28.306 --> 00:00:37.063
cpp is a foundational, highly portable inference project with extensive control over quantized models, CPU execution, and several GPU backends.

00:00:37.063 --> 00:00:44.190
It is useful when you need explicit tuning or want to understand the underlying inference options.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:52.947
Open WebUI adds a browser-based conversation layer and can connect to backends such as Ollama or compatible local API servers.

00:00:52.947 --> 00:01:00.482
Text-generation-webui offers a broad set of loaders and controls, but its flexibility also creates more configuration choices.

00:01:00.482 --> 00:01:08.831
Select a tool because it supports a defined use case, not because it exposes the largest number of switches.

00:01:08.831 --> 00:01:17.180
Local API servers allow editors, scripts, retrieval systems, and other applications to call the model through a consistent interface.

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:24.308
Start by binding the service to the loopback address so only the workstation can reach it.

00:01:24.308 --> 00:01:34.693
Test a single client, confirm authentication options if remote access is later required, and document the model name, port, context settings, and startup method.

00:01:34.693 --> 00:01:38.155
Avoid unnecessary orchestration during the first pass.

00:01:38.155 --> 00:01:44.468
Multiple front ends, containers, proxy layers, and model servers make failures harder to isolate.

00:01:44.468 --> 00:01:49.559
Establish a simple path from model file to successful accelerated response.

00:01:49.559 --> 00:01:56.687
Once that path is measured and repeatable, add interfaces or automation one component at a time.

00:01:56.687 --> 00:02:04.221
Simplicity at the beginning is not a limitation; it is a controlled baseline for everything that follows.
